; REQUEST-09 under Phase 2.3 (nominal-per-instantiation): a dep whose own spec produces a
; collapsed-set shape through generic instances at field sites (`set<key_hash>` /
; `nonempty_set<key_hash>`). Each instance now NOMINALIZES — `set<key_hash>` mints its own
; `SetKeyHash` wasm class — but the STRUCTURAL boundary wrapper (`KeyHashList` /
; `NonEmptyKeyHashList`) still exists (it is the nominal's `new()`/`get()` boundary, and the inline
; `[* key_hash]` mints it too), so a consumer's `--wrapper-requests` for that structural shape is
; STILL satisfied from own-spec — the re-key to nominal classes does not strand the structural row.
;
; The generic defs carry the explicit `; @duplicates preserve` opt-out: tag 258 now defaults to
; `@duplicates reject` (the well-known-tag registry), which would give the nominals an `OrderedSet`
; inner and a different boundary wrapper. The satisfied-from-own-spec behavior under test is
; orthogonal to the duplicates policy, so the fixture stays on the plain `Vec` representation.
key_hash = bytes ; @newtype
set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0] ; @duplicates preserve
nonempty_set<a0> = #6.258([+ a0]) / [+ a0] ; @duplicates preserve
cert = [pool_owners: set<key_hash>, extra: [* key_hash]]
signers = [required: nonempty_set<key_hash>]
